Looking at the net, I'll track how the vertices merge when folded into an octahedron with vertices {T, B, N, E, S, W}.

- Starting with the middle triangle (P3,P4,P6) → (T,N,E).
- Folding upward: triangle (P3,P2,P4) → (T,W,N); triangle (P1,P2,P3) → (S,W,T); triangle (P2,P5,P4) → (W,B,N).
- Folding downward: triangle (P4,P7,P6) → (N,B,E); triangle (P6,P7,P9) → (E,B,S); triangle (P8,P6,P9) → (T,E,S); triangle (P9,P7,P10) → (S,B,W).

Now the labelled edges map to octahedron edges:
- x = (P1,P2) → {S,W}
- C = (P1,P3) → {S,T}
- E = (P3,P6) → {T,E}
- D = (P8,P6) → {T,E}
- A = (P8,P9) → {T,S}
- B = (P9,P10) → {S,W}

Edge x ({S,W}) coincides with edge B ({S,W}).

\boxed{B}
